      q: "A research scientist purifies DNA polymerase III from an Escherichia coli extract. The isolated enzymes are then incubated in a mixture containing DNA templates, RNA primer oligonucleotides, and tagged deoxynucleotides. After analyzing the DNA molecules formed during incubation, the researcher concludes that the enzyme possesses 3′ to 5′ exonuclease activity.\n\nWhich of the following enzymatic actions was most likely observed during the experiment?",
